      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-213015",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $A$ and $B$ are sets, and $U$ is a universal set. Prove that\n$A\u2229B^(\u2015) = A^(\u2015)\u222aB^(\u2015)$.\n\nGiven an element $x \u2208 U$, we have the following sequence of equivalent statements:\n$x \u2209 A\u222aB$ {{field-1}}"
