      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222193",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following statement:\n\n> Given that $A$ and $B$ are sets, $A\u222aB^(\u2015) = A^(\u2015)\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n\nA proof of this statement is given below.\n\n> $L1$: $x \u2208 A\u222aB^(\u2015)$\n> $L2$: $\u21d4x \u2209 A\u222aB$\n> $L3$: $\u21d4\u00ac(x \u2208 A\u222aB)$\n> $L4$: $\u21d4\u00ac((x \u2208 A)\u2228(x \u2208 B))$\n> $L5$: $\u21d4(\u00ac(x \u2208 A))\u2227(\u00ac(x \u2208 B))$\n> $L6$: $\u21d4(x \u2209 A)\u2227(x \u2209 B)$\n> $L7$: $\u21d4(x \u2208 A^(\u2015))\u2227(x \u2208 B^(\u2015))$\n> $L8$: $\u21d4x \u2208 A^(\u2015)\u2229B^(\u2015)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L3$ follows from line $L2$ by the definition of {{field-1}}\n\nLine $L7$ follows from line $L6$ by the definition of {{field-2}}\n\nLine $L8$ follows from line $L7$ by the definition of {{field-3}}"
    },
